---
// Terms of Use. The copy is transferred verbatim from the version previously
// hosted on Firebase — legal text is not paraphrased, and any change here is a
// change to a published policy, so edit deliberately and bump LAST_UPDATED.
//
// Moved onto the apex domain because legal pages on a different host are a weak
// trust signal, and because these now appear in the sitemap like any other page.
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { LEGAL_CONTACT_EMAIL, LEGAL_LAST_UPDATED } from '../consts';

const updated = new Date(LEGAL_LAST_UPDATED).toLocaleDateString('en-GB', {
  day: 'numeric', month: 'long', year: 'numeric', timeZone: 'UTC',
});
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Use"
  description="The terms for using Cirrus, the quit vaping app: who can use it, what it is and is not, community rules, subscriptions and how to end it."
  breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Terms' }]}
>
  <div class="wrap page">
    <article class="prose legal">
      <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
      <p class="post-meta">Last updated {updated}</p>

<p class="lede">These are the terms for using Cirrus. Using the app means you
  accept them.</p>

  <h2>Who can use it</h2>
  <p>You must be 18 or over. Cirrus is about reducing and stopping nicotine
  use; it is not appropriate for minors, and the app will not let you continue
  setup if you tell us you are under 18.</p>

  <h2>What Cirrus is, and is not</h2>
  <p>Cirrus is a self-help tool: it tracks what you log, calculates a tapering
  plan from it, and gives you a coach to talk to. <strong>It is not medical
  treatment, and it does not replace a doctor, a pharmacist, or a quitline.</strong>
  Ember, the in-app coach, is a language model. It will not give you medical
  advice, dosing guidance, or a diagnosis, and you should not treat anything it
  says as any of those.</p>
  <p>If you are in crisis, please contact your local emergency services. In the
  US and Canada you can call or text 988 at any time.</p>

  <h2>Your account</h2>
  <p>Keep your login details to yourself; you are responsible for what happens
  under your account. Tell us if you think someone else has access to it.</p>

  <h2>The community</h2>
  <p>The feed is anonymous but it is not unmoderated. When you post you agree
  not to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>harass, threaten, or abuse anyone;</li>
    <li>name brands, recommend products, or tell people where to buy nicotine;</li>
    <li>give medical or dosing advice;</li>
    <li>post anything illegal, hateful, or sexual;</li>
    <li>share anyone's personal information, including your own.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Posts are screened automatically before they appear and reviewed by a
  person when flagged. We aim to review reported content within 24 hours. We
  can remove content and suspend accounts that break these rules. You can
  report or block from any post.</p>
  <p>You keep ownership of what you write. You give us permission to display it
  in the app and to keep it visible in a thread if you later delete your
  account, detached from you and re-attributed anonymously, so that a
  conversation other people are part of stays readable.</p>

  <h2>Subscriptions</h2>
  <p>Cirrus has a free tier that keeps working indefinitely. Some features are
  part of a paid subscription.</p>
  <p>Where subscriptions are available, they are billed through the app store
  you installed from, on the plan and price shown before you confirm. They
  renew automatically at the end of each period unless you cancel at least 24
  hours before it ends. Manage or cancel in your store account settings — not
  here; we cannot cancel a store subscription for you. If a free trial is
  offered, any unused part of it ends when you subscribe. Refunds are handled
  by the store under its own policy.</p>

  <h2>Availability</h2>
  <p>We do our best to keep Cirrus working, but we do not promise it will
  always be available or error-free. Features may change. We may need to
  suspend the service for maintenance.</p>

  <h2>Limits</h2>
  <p>Cirrus is provided as-is. To the extent the law allows, we are not liable
  for indirect or consequential loss arising from your use of it. Nothing here
  limits liability that cannot legally be limited — including for death or
  personal injury caused by negligence, or for fraud.</p>

  <h2>Ending it</h2>
  <p>You can stop using Cirrus and delete your account at any time from
  Settings. We may suspend or end access if these terms are broken.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>If we change these terms materially we will say so in the app before the
  change takes effect.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p><a href={`mailto:${LEGAL_CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{LEGAL_CONTACT_EMAIL}</a></p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
